{
 "id": "core", "version": "0.8",
 "license": "GPL-2.0-or-later",
 "title": "core", "category": "Framework", "author": "irpina, Iced-Cream",
 "description": "The boot copier, the hook bus and mod storage for the Analog Four MKII: every other mod needs it. The Digitakt mk1's core.s, settings.s and render.s with the A4's addresses, as core-ar2 builds them for the Analog Rytm MKII, store.c: fields mods declare, placed by elekloader from the build's lockfile and kept in bytes stock never uses or always holds at 0; from 0.2, pages.s: the four routines every parameter page goes through, asked through core_pages and core_params (and from 0.3 core_page_fns, a page whose knobs follow the sound), and views behind the page keys through core_view_pages, and core-ar2's load.s: the audio interrupt's load. On its own it changes nothing the unit does. And core-ar2's finish.s: an OS upgrade's restart sends the panel link's and the UART's queued bytes before it masks interrupts, where stock can hang on SUCCESS! REBOOTING. From 0.5 the lock service's first part: lockable parameters with codes per track kind (lock.c) and their p-locks as lock rows in each pattern, kept in a ledger that follows stock's step records, with the playing trig's locks and Param Slide's deltas per voice (rows.c, rows.s); and its second part, destinations: mod parameters at the end of every route, Dest, macro and CONTROL IN list of their track kind, their codes kept in those bytes, their names on the knobs, lists and setup screens, and per voice the sources pointing at them, noted at each of stock's pushes (dests.c, dests.s). And its third part, the value read: core_param_values, the value stock would play for a lockable parameter, in stock's stages and order with its clamps, from the inputs of the block taken at ev_render_out, per voice, with the track read on the last-played voice (value.c). And its fourth part, MIDI: each mod parameter is NRPN MSB 0, LSB its code, on its track's channel, and a field declared \"cc\": true also gets a CC stock leaves unused there; both set it as its knob does, and a mod knob's turn sends it as stock's parameter out sends its own (midi.c, midi.s). From 0.6 core-ar2 0.10..0.13's foundations: a field's init (core_field_inits), the project's modified mark after mod-only edits (core_project_edited), ev_project_save around every whole project save, payloads (core_payloads) in a mods' area of 37.7 MB from 0x45650000, knob looks for mod knob ids (core_knob_looks; looks.c, looks.s) and the screen calls (screen.c): text in stock's fonts, a key handed to stock, overlays, the level readout and the progress box. From 0.7 the standard events (std1) at the sites core owns, through its std map: ev_boot, ev_tick, ev_draw, ev_key, ev_settings, ev_project, ev_render_in and ev_param_turn, with core_redraw, core_post and core_timer (std.c), and ev_settings' core_setting_add and ev_draw's core_px, core_fill, core_text and core_blit (std.c, stdui.s); and at new sites (stdmidi.c, stdmidi.s) ev_midi_in, ev_sysex_in, ev_midi_cc, ev_midi_pc, ev_midi_out, ev_seq_midi and ev_seq_tick; and ev_voice_start and ev_voice_end in the audio interrupt (voice.c, voice.s); and at new sites the UI and system events ev_boot_done, ev_idle, ev_crash, ev_usb, ev_key_leds (core_led_set), ev_mode, ev_param_set, ev_clip, ev_pattern (the change and, before it, the request) and ev_mute, ev_view (the view stack's pushes and removes), and the A4's own ev_knob_turn, every page knob turn with which edit it becomes and the LEVEL encoder's and mixer page's level turns, and ev_analog_frame, the analog frame before it is packed, and ev_mod_set, a modulation slot's destination or depth on the VELOCITY, MOD WHEEL, PITCH BEND, BREATH, AFTERTOUCH and PERF setups (ui.c, ui.s). From 0.8 the A4's own ev_track_key, a key the sequencer view handles, with the view, and its helpers core_track_held, core_track_current, core_track_pattern and core_popup (trackkey.c, trackkey.s); ev_voice_params, the voices' parameter words after modulation, before the analog frame is built from them; and ev_sound_setup, SOUND SETUP's rows, with core_sound_setup_toggle (sound.c, sound.s). And room for +Drive mods: spare entries in its tables for an A4 Drive Loader to fill at boot, ev_boot_drive, once in main() after the +Drive is up and before the boot's project load, the audio interrupt and the UI task, where the Drive Loader may set the live layout in core_store_ids and core_store_gens (the live generations) that the boot's load then reads with, and ev_drive_format, in FORMAT +DRIVE after the slot erases; and core_restart, a reboot from a task once the +Drive is idle and the panel link and UART have sent what they hold, and core_restart_now (restart.s). And \"handle\": true storage fields, walked by core_handle_fields (store.c), the table core_handles the Drive Loader adds its handle fields to.",
 "device": "analog-four-mk2", "os": "1.56",
 "sources": ["../core/core.s", "../core/settings.s", "../core/render.s", "store.c", "store.s", "pages.s", "lock.c", "rows.c", "rows.s", "dests.c", "dests.s", "value.c", "midi.c", "midi.s", "../core-ar2/load.s", "../core-ar2/finish.s", "restart.s", "../core-ar2/payload.c", "looks.c", "looks.s", "screen.c", "std.c", "stdui.s", "stdmidi.c", "stdmidi.s", "voice.c", "voice.s", "ui.c", "ui.s", "trackkey.c", "trackkey.s", "sound.c", "sound.s"],
